one codebase: forum-for-nerds, a self-hosted Next.js forum plus blog running on pure Docker with SQLite for dev and MariaDB in prod. Ten dead forums walked in, one nerd forum walked out.\\\\r\\\\n For storage I ended up with OneDrive 365 Basic with 100 GB for 2 euros a month, after years of being convinced I'd never give Microsoft a cent, until the Windows and Samsung integration won me over.\\\\r\\\\n Speed doesn't matter much to me, and if OneDrive ever offers a 500 GB cold archive tier on very slow old hard drives for one or two euros a month, I'd be the first customer, and I'd probably store all my photos there too since 100 GB is easily enough for me.\\\\r\\\\n I never actually needed it, since I never used more than two or three GB, but now I just upload 30 GB so I can say I use it.\\\\r\\\\n===CURRENT mentions check===\\\\r\\\\ninfra-pilot in current: True\\\\r\\\\nstreuland in current: False\\\\r\\\\nforgecms in current: True\\\\r\\\\nForgeCMS in current: True\\\\r\\\\nai-chat-webui in current: False\\\\r\\\\nstranded-horizons in current: False\\\\r\\\\ncooperating-screen in current: False\\\\r\\\\ned-docs in current: False\\\\r\\\\naktienwerk in current: False\\\\r\\\\nforum-for-nerds in current: True\\\\r\\\\n===OLDEST README===\\\\r\\\\n- 👋 Hi, I’m @DaaanielTV\\\\r\\\\n- 👀 I’m interested in tech and ai\\\\r\\\\n- 🌱 I’m currently learning python and java\\\\r\\\\n- 💞️ I’m looking to collaborate on my minecraft server\\\\r\\\\n- 📫 How to reach me discord: daaanieltv\\\\r\\\\n- 😄 Pronouns: he/his\\\\r\\\\n- ⚡ Fun fact: doing stuff with debian since 2018\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n<!---\\\\r\\\\nDaaanielTV/DaaanielTV is a ✨ special ✨ repository because its `README.md` (this file) appears on your GitHub profile.\\\\r\\\\nYou can click the Preview link to take a look at your changes.\\\\r\\\\n--->\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 3007,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 752,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\"}","truncated":false}
